  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the minimum probability of any outcome in each lottery and prefers the one with the higher such minimum. In this case, Lottery A has a minimum probability of 100%, Lottery B of 20%, so the reason favors A. The individual in the verbal report emphasizes the certainty of A and the non-negligible chance of getting nothing in B — this aligns with attending to the lowest-probability-or-outcome-risk, particularly the 20% chance of nothing in B. While the individual does not explicitly mention 'minimum probability' as a formal rule, the emphasis on the risk of zero in B and the certainty in A reflects a consideration of outcome security that closely corresponds to the core idea of the decision reason. The justification, though phrased in natural language and including additional elements (e.g., magnitude of gain), is consistent with the logic of preferring the lottery with higher minimum probability. Therefore, the information considered and the justification align sufficiently with the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

